            "request_id": "83e0dfb8-aa96-4b3a-8846-d9b1fd00935b",
            "answer": "**Auto Loader\u202f\u2014\u202fIncremental, scalable ingestion on Databricks**\n\n| Aspect | What Auto Loader does | Why it matters |\n|--------|----------------------|----------------|\n| **Core concept** | Provides a Structured Streaming source called `cloudFiles` that continuously discovers and reads new files as they land in cloud storage. | Eliminates the need for custom file\u2011listing loops and gives exactly\u2011once processing. |\n| **Supported storage** | Amazon S3 (`s3://`), Azure Data Lake Storage (`abfss://`), Google Cloud Storage (`gs://`), Unity Catalog volumes (`/Volumes/`), Azure Blob (`wasbs://`). | Works natively with the major cloud object stores used on Databricks. |\n| **File formats** | JSON, CSV, XML, Parquet, Avro, ORC, TEXT, BINARYFILE (including pre\u2011compressed variants). | Handles most common analytics data without extra conversion steps. |\n| **Progress tracking** | As files are discovered, their metadata is stored in a RocksDB key\u2011value store located in the pipeline\u2019s checkpoint directory. This guarantees exactly\u2011once semantics and automatic recovery after failures. | No manual state management; fault\u2011tolerant streaming. |\n| **File\u2011detection modes** | *Directory\u2011listing mode* (default) \u2013 periodically lists objects in the path.<br>*File\u2011notification mode* \u2013 uses cloud\u2011native event notifications (S3 EventBridge, Azure Event Grid, GCS Pub/Sub). Databricks recommends the notification mode for most workloads because it reduces latency and cloud\u2011API costs. | Choose the mode that matches your latency and cost requirements. |\n| **Schema handling** | Auto\u2011infers schema on first read and can evolve it automatically (add new columns, type widening) while preserving existing data. | Reduces operational overhead when source schemas change. |\n| **Production\u2011ready settings** | \u2022 Checkpointing (managed automatically in Lakeflow pipelines).<br>\u2022 Error handling & file\u2011retention policies.<br>\u2022 Tomb\u2011stone retention for CDC pipelines.<br>\u2022 Monitoring metrics (files discovered, ingestion latency, etc.). | Provides reliability, observability, and cost\u2011control for long\u2011running pipelines. |\n| **Benefits vs. raw Structured Streaming** | \u2022 **Scalability** \u2013 can discover billions of files efficiently.<br>\u2022 **Performance** \u2013 discovery cost scales with number of files ingested, not number of directories.<br>\u2022 **Cost** \u2013 native cloud APIs and optional notification mode avoid expensive directory scans.<br>\u2022 **Schema evolution** \u2013 automatic drift detection and rescue. | Makes large\u2011scale, near\u2011real\u2011time ingestion practical and cheaper. |\n\n### Typical usage pattern (Python)\n\n```python\n# Example: ingest JSON files from an S3 bucket into a Delta table\ndf = (spark.readStream\n          .format(\"cloudFiles\")\n          .option(\"cloudFiles.format\", \"json\")          # file format\n          .option(\"cloudFiles.schemaLocation\", \"/tmp/checkpoint/schema\")  # optional schema cache\n          .load(\"s3://my-bucket/raw-data/\"))\n\n# Write incrementally to a Delta table\n(df.writeStream\n   .format(\"delta\")\n   .option(\"checkpointLocation\", \"/tmp/checkpoint/delta\")\n   .table(\"my_db.raw_events\"))\n```\n\n*When used inside a Lakeflow pipeline, you can omit the explicit schema and checkpoint options because the pipeline manages them automatically.*\n\n### Where to read more\n\n- Overview of Auto Loader, supported sources & formats, and how it works: <https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/ingestion/cloud-object-storage/auto-loader/>\u3010Source 1\u3011  \n- Production\u2011workload recommendations (checkpointing, error handling, file\u2011notification mode, etc.): <https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/ingestion/cloud-object-storage/auto-loader/>\u3010Source 3\u3011\n\n**In short**, Auto Loader turns cloud object storage into a reliable, exactly\u2011once streaming source that scales to billions of files, automatically handles schema changes, and offers production\u2011grade controls for cost, latency, and observability.",
